<title>SPAIN: Spain Nov CPI flat vs Oct, yr/yr falls to 3.2 pct.</title>
<headline>Spain Nov CPI flat vs Oct, yr/yr falls to 3.2 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Statistics Institute (INE) gave the following figures:</p>
<p> SPANISH INFLATION		NOV 96    OCT 96    NOV 95</p>
<p> Monthly CPI index change	0.0	  0.1	 0.3</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.2	  3.5	 4.4</p>
<p> Core inflation		    0.0	  0.2	 0.1</p>
<p> Year-on-year rise		 3.1	  3.2	 4.8</p>
<p> INDEX BY COMPONENTS	     NOV 96    OCT  96     YR/YR</p>
<p> Food				  -0.1	 -0.3	 3.0</p>
<p> Clothing			     0.4	  0.5	 2.3</p>
<p> Housing				0.4	  0.7	 4.5</p>
<p> Household goods		    0.0	  0.1	 3.8</p>
<p> Medicine			     0.0	  0.2	 3.6</p>
<p> Transport			    0.0	  0.3	 3.0</p>
<p> Culture				0.1	  0.6	 2.7</p>
<p> Other				 -0.4	 -0.1	 3.7</p>
<p>Note - In food, fresh food fell 0.1 pct from the previous month (2.5 pct year-on-year) and processed food fell 0.1 (3.3 pct year-on-year)</p>
</text>
